---
description: How Flick reaches its public URL
alwaysApply: true
---

Pushing `main` to GitHub (`ShaharShokrani/flick`) publishes
https://temporary-brisk-mesa-ty777ur.vercel.app/ — that repo is
connected to the Vercel project, so a push is the deploy.

Do not run the Vercel CLI from this machine. The project is claimed on
the owner's account and the anonymous session is dead, so
`vercel deploy` and `npm run deploy` cannot work without a
`VERCEL_TOKEN`. `.githooks/pre-push` skips the attempt unless that token
is set. Retrying it only burns time.

This machine also cannot set Vercel environment variables. When
production needs one, verify with `curl -sS <host>/api/health/db` and
tell the owner the exact variable and value to set.

Never commit `.vercel/`, Vercel tokens, or connection strings.
